\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a)~Sequential pipelines address judge bias and contamination independently; omitted variable bias confounds the unmodeled facet into ability estimates. (b)~G-MFRM three-stage joint calibration: Stage~1 fits a standard MFRM for initial estimates $(\hat  {\theta }, \hat  {b}, \hat  {d})$; Stage~2 estimates per-item exposure $e_i$ from external evidence (reference model anchoring, cross-model agreement, and optionally LogProber); Stage~3 performs joint MCMC inference with $e_i$ fixed, recovering contamination-corrected ability $\hat  {\theta }_n$, contamination susceptibility $c_n$, and judge severity $d_j$.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{2}{(a)~Sequential pipelines address judge bias and contamination independently; omitted variable bias confounds the unmodeled facet into ability estimates. (b)~G-MFRM three-stage joint calibration: Stage~1 fits a standard MFRM for initial estimates $(\hat {\theta }, \hat {b}, \hat {d})$; Stage~2 estimates per-item exposure $e_i$ from external evidence (reference model anchoring, cross-model agreement, and optionally LogProber); Stage~3 performs joint MCMC inference with $e_i$ fixed, recovering contamination-corrected ability $\hat {\theta }_n$, contamination susceptibility $c_n$, and judge severity $d_j$}{figure.caption.1}{}}
