\newlabel{tab:bias_absorption}{{7}{16}{Contamination bias absorption in MFRM-only estimation. $\Delta \theta = \hat {\theta }_{\text {MFRM}} - \hat {\theta }_{\text {G-MFRM}}$. Models with high contamination susceptibility ($c_n$) have inflated ability estimates under MFRM-only; models with low $c_n$ are relatively deflated. The perfect rank correlation (Spearman $\rho = 1.0$) between $\Delta \theta $ and $c_n$ empirically confirms the omitted variable bias predicted in Section~\ref {sec:confounding}}{table.caption.48}{}}
